# NorthSound Cumulus Services SQL ARM update

This package keeps the earlier speed-focused cleanup that removed Static Web App and Application Insights, then adds Azure SQL to the ARM template.

## Added to the ARM template

The ARM template now creates the following SQL resources when `deploySqlResources` is `true`:

- Azure SQL logical server: `sql-nscs-platform-<suffix>`
- Optional Azure SQL Database: `sqldb-customer-index`
- SQL firewall rule: `AllowAzureServices`

The optional database is intentionally lightweight and does not use `sampleName = AdventureWorksLT`. That avoids reintroducing the slower sample database deployment path from the old LCA.

## New ARM parameters

- `deploySqlResources` defaults to `true`.
- `deploySqlDatabase` defaults to `true`.
- `sqlAdministratorLogin` defaults to `nscsadmin`.
- `sqlAdministratorPassword` defaults to `@lab.CloudPortalCredential(User1).Password`.
- `sqlDatabaseName` defaults to `sqldb-customer-index`.

If Skillable does not token-replace the secure string default in your ARM deployment flow, pass `sqlAdministratorPassword` explicitly through the template parameters file.

## Updated scripts

- The evidence seeding script now discovers `sql-nscs-platform-*` and includes SQL server details, plus database details when the optional database exists, in the evidence summary, deployment log, incident notes, and investigation guide.
- The validation LCA now checks for the SQL logical server. It does not require the optional database, so you can set `deploySqlDatabase` to `false` without breaking validation.
- The management-plane activity LCA now tags the SQL server as platform metadata during activity generation.

## Recommendation

Remove or disable the old `Deploy sample database` LCA if you enable SQL in this ARM template. Keeping both will create duplicate SQL work and may slow the lab down.
